### Previews & Verification Commands

To capture previews or verify that your infrastructure matches the expected state, you can run the following diagnostic commands in your terminal (`/home/bob/terraform`):

#### 1. Plan Verification
Ensure `terraform plan` reports clean execution with no drift:
```bash
terraform plan
Expected Output:
No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.

2. AWS CLI Verification Previews
Verify AMI Status:

Bash
aws ec2 describe-images \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --owners self \
  --filters "Name=name,Values=devops-ec2-ami" \
  --query 'Images[].{Name:Name,ImageId:ImageId,State:State}' \
  --output table
Verify New Instance Status:

Bash
aws ec2 describe-instances \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=devops-ec2-new" \
  --query 'Reservations[].Instances[].{Name:Tags[?Key==`Name`].Value|[0],InstanceId:InstanceId,ImageId:ImageId,State:State.Name}' \
  --output table
